# E2E contract

Portable scenarios live in `functional-tests/flows/`. Drivers (React Playwright/RTL, optional Java model) consume the same YAML.

## Select

- Visible text, labels, roles, and `data-testid`
- `data-testid` values must match `functional-tests/control-ids.md`
- Never select by Swing class, CSS-in-JS hash, XPath, or React component name

## Assert

- User-visible outcomes and kernel oracles: aliases, entry type, dirty, file exists, `reopenSucceeds` (kernel load of saved bytes), `errorId`, dialog shown
- Do not assert DOM structure that would differ between toolkits
- Do not assert JCA/BouncyCastle bag-for-bag equality; that remains JUnit on `kse/`. SPA tests must still round-trip PKCS#12 the kernel wrote.

## Write

- No `JButton` / `JFileChooser` / CSS in YAML `when`/`then`
- Unknown fixture passwords: `blocked`, never guessed
- `P3.schema` owns `when`/`then` and `control-ids.md`. Slice YAML must not introduce undocumented commands.

Scenarios must set `slice` (`kernel` \| `file` \| `generate` \| `import` \| `delete-rename` \| `details` \| `export` \| `sign` \| `verify-sig` \| `examine` \| `clipboard` \| `chain` \| `session` \| `chrome`) and `requires` (list of slice ids that must already be implemented). File-slice runners load `slice: file` with empty `requires`. Kernel coverage is primarily `frontend/src/kernel/` tests plus save/reopen oracles.
